# Task
Generate a short, memorable title for an organizational goal.

You will be given a full goal description. Generate a single short title (1-2 words) that captures the essence of this goal and can be used as shorthand in conversation and documentation.

## Guidelines

- Output exactly 1-2 words
- Professional and sophisticated tone
- Easy to pronounce (prefer 2-3 syllables per word)
- Contain alphabetic characters only (no emojis, punctuation, or special characters)
- Capture the core intent or outcome, not the method
- Be distinctive and memorable
- Avoid generic corporate jargon
- Prefer active verbs or concrete nouns
- The title should feel natural to say: "How's [Title] going?" or "We're focused on [Title] this week"
- Goal titles must be unique within the organization - do not reuse existing titles
- Avoid titles that are too similar to existing ones, even if not identical

## Existing Goal Titles to Avoid

{% for goal in other_goals %}
- {{ goal.title }}
{% endfor %}

## Examples

Goal: "Ship a Q1 roadmap we're proud of"
Title: Velocity

Goal: "Customers are actively using goals to run their business"
Title: Adoption

Goal: "Make sure early customers stick and get value"
Title: Retention

Goal: "Acquire our first meaningful set of paying customers"
Title: Conversion

Goal: "Figure out how customers find and buy from us"
Title: Discover

Goal: "New features become part of how customers operate"
Title: Integration
